---
/**
 * Related card for the Naha drainage. Self-contained so it can move if the
 * first project changes from tidewater to Shelter Cove Road.
 */
---

<a
  href="/projects/naha-connector"
  class="block border border-contour bg-sheet p-5 transition hover:border-ink md:p-6"
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Featured project · Shelter Cove → Loring</p>
  <h3 class="headline mt-3 text-2xl">The Naha Connector</h3>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/85">
    The State opened Shelter Cove Road in October 2025, then stopped at the edge of a
    roadless area written to accommodate recreation access. Two trail segments would
    complete the first walk-in route from Ketchikan's road system to the Naha's cabins and
    the National Recreation Trail down to Loring.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-tide">
    Read the project →
  </p>
</a>
